    "result_text": "The only concrete test class is `AcceptanceTest` (the other two are the abstract base and a support class). All tests pass and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` field \u2014 `EMAIL` when the owner has an email, otherwise `PHONE` \u2014 as a computed, read-only field on the owner response.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `contactPreference` property (enum `EMAIL`/`PHONE`) to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator produces `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum` and the getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that derives it: `owner.getEmail() == null || owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? PHONE : EMAIL`. This matches the existing email-presence convention used by `MembershipLevels.of(...)`, and because it's derived from the persisted email, the create response and any later `GET /api/owners/{id}` compute the same value.\n\nNo new OfficeFloor function/YAML was needed: the value is a pure mapping of the persisted `Owner`, and `RespondWithOwner` already serializes via `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, consistent with how the sibling derived fields (`membershipLevel`, `locality`, etc.) are handled.\n\n**Verification:** Both new acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) pass, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests, 0 failures).",
